    "result_text": "All 293 tests pass, including the new Cp18 test. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field on owner creation following the same pattern already established for the transient `namesakeCount` and `sharesHousehold` fields.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` string property (enum `local`/`remote`) to the `Owner` (`OwnerDto`) response schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` `locality` field with getter/setter (computed at creation, not persisted).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, set `owner.setLocality(resolveLocality(owner.getCity()))` before saving. The new `resolveLocality` helper groups existing owners' cities case-insensitively, finds the max count, and returns `\"local\"` only if the owner's city is the **single** most common city among existing owners \u2014 otherwise `\"remote\"` (including when there are no owners or when there's a tie for most common).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an explicit `locality` mapping. The default MapStruct `String`\u2192enum conversion uses `Enum.valueOf` (matching the constant name `LOCAL`), which threw an `IllegalArgumentException` for the lowercase JSON value `\"local\"`. The new `toLocality` helper resolves via `LocalityEnum.fromValue()` instead, matching on the JSON value.\n\nThe `Cp18Tests` acceptance test now passes, and the full suite (293 tests) remains green.",
